WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.652
In under two minutes, you will put your own lights on the map.

00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:04.684
We start on the map.

00:00:05.585 --> 00:00:08.917
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:10.953 --> 00:00:13.376
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:13.376 --> 00:00:15.866
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:15.866 --> 00:00:17.211
Tap Use my location.

00:00:18.951 --> 00:00:21.167
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:21.819
Tap Allow.

00:00:25.337 --> 00:00:27.833
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:27.833 --> 00:00:29.051
See the three dots?

00:00:29.051 --> 00:00:29.598
Tap them.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.780
In the menu, tap Add.

00:00:34.539 --> 00:00:35.955
Tap A lighting display.

00:00:37.898 --> 00:00:39.116
Who is posting?

00:00:39.116 --> 00:00:40.409
Tap A homeowner.

00:00:40.409 --> 00:00:41.474
Then tap Next.

00:00:44.009 --> 00:00:45.611
Type the name to show.

00:00:45.611 --> 00:00:46.587
Then tap Next.

00:00:49.281 --> 00:00:51.516
Did a company install your lights?

00:00:51.516 --> 00:00:52.857
We did it ourselves.

00:00:52.857 --> 00:00:54.007
Tap No, then Next.

00:00:56.536 --> 00:00:57.503
Which season?

00:00:57.503 --> 00:00:59.229
Tap Christmas, then Next.

00:01:01.753 --> 00:01:05.114
Name the display, and tell us what makes it special.

00:01:05.114 --> 00:01:06.002
Then tap Next.

00:01:11.097 --> 00:01:12.443
Add the address.

00:01:12.443 --> 00:01:13.947
The pin goes here.

00:01:13.947 --> 00:01:15.056
Then tap Next.

00:01:18.825 --> 00:01:22.353
Tell families when the lights are on, and how to see them.

00:01:22.353 --> 00:01:23.190
Then tap Next.

00:01:26.293 --> 00:01:27.456
Add photos.

00:01:27.456 --> 00:01:28.812
Then tap Next.

00:01:31.685 --> 00:01:34.123
Check everything, and tap Put it on the map.

00:01:36.151 --> 00:01:38.345
Next up: Find lights near you.
